      passage: `Many famous and successful people had very simple jobs before they became famous, and I think their stories are inspiring.\n\nBefore he was a famous actor, Brad Pitt dressed up as a chicken to advertise a restaurant called El Pollo Loco! He stood outside the restaurant in a big chicken costume, waving at cars, and he says it was one of the most embarrassing jobs he ever had.\n\nThe singer Rihanna worked as a shop assistant in a clothes shop in her home country, Barbados, before she became a music star. She has said that job taught her how to talk to people and sell things, which helped her a lot later in her career.\n\nBefore he became one of the richest men in the world, Jeff Bezos, the founder of Amazon, worked at McDonald's when he was a teenager. He cooked burgers and cleaned tables, just like millions of other teenagers around the world.\n\nThe actress Whoopi Goldberg worked as a bricklayer and also styled hair in a funeral home before she became famous for acting and comedy. She often jokes about how different her life is now compared to those early jobs.\n\nThese stories show that everyone starts somewhere, often with a simple, ordinary job. Your first job doesn't decide your whole future — it's just the beginning of your story, and you never know where you might end up!`,
